<title>MEXICO: Mexico Bondes rate falls slightly at auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico Bondes rate falls slightly at auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rate on Mexican government 728-day development bonds, or Bondes, fell 0.28 percentage points to 1.07 percent above the 28-day Cetes rate in Tuesday's primary auction, dealers estimated.</p>
<p>The 728-day Bondes were assigned at 98.30704 pesos.</p>
<p>Demand for the bondes was 4.052 billion pesos, compared with the 800 million offered by the Banco de Mexico.</p>
<p>- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559</p>
